<title>UK: BOE gives UK money market 151 mln stg further help.</title>
<headline>BOE gives UK money market 151 mln stg further help.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of England said it provided the UK money market with a further 151 million stg of assistance at established interest rates.</p>
<p>			     EARLY	1200 GMT   1400 GMT   LATE</p>
<p> FORECAST SHORTAGE     1.05 BLN   900 MLN    700 MLN    =</p>
<p> CUMULATIVE SUPPLY     74 MLN     499 MLN    650 MLN    =</p>
<p>DETAILS</p>
<p> BILLS/FRG TO MARCH 3  74 MLN#    215 MLN#   =	    =</p>
<p> BAND 1 BANK BILLS	=	   160 MLN*   80 MLN*    =</p>
<p> BAND 2 BANK BILLS	=	   50  MLN*   71 MLN*    =</p>
<p># INTEREST RATE - 5-31/32 PCT (INDICATES UNCHANGED BASE RATES)</p>
<p>* INTEREST RATE - 5-15/16 PCT</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7708</p>
